  "step_by_step_reasoning": "The whiteboard architecture depicts a real-time IoT sports telemetry processing pipeline. Smart sports equipment with embedded sensors sends movement/telemetry data directly into Kinesis Data Stream. From Kinesis Data Stream, data splits into two parallel flows: 1) Streamed into Kinesis Firehose and stored in S3 for long-term data lake storage and model development, and 2) Streamed into AWS Lambda for real-time ML inference and segmentation. Lambda writes processed analytics into DynamoDB, which serves AWS AppSync. AppSync then provides real-time WebSockets/GraphQL updates to end-user applications (fans/broadcasters). Cognito is present on the whiteboard for user authentication.",
